{{ ref: e1cbaaf7-f9b6-4d68-9181-a3da4db66b18 }}
- **Scope**: The `core` crate's graph foundation — identifier interning, CSR adjacency, iterative Tarjan condensation, and longest-path layering — plus property tests and a 100k-node release benchmark. No language knowledge, no I/O.
--{ ref: e1cbaaf7-f9b6-4d68-9181-a3da4db66b18 }--
{{ ref: 2ccc5581-0751-4d7b-8c82-c5ff2f842f0e }}
- **Description**: Deterministic, linear-time base for every later solver phase. The custom CSR layout (AD-6) gives cache-friendly forward and reverse adjacency; Tarjan uses an explicit stack so 100k-node chains cannot overflow; SCCs come out in reverse topological order, making the condensation deterministic across runs and thread counts.
--{ ref: 2ccc5581-0751-4d7b-8c82-c5ff2f842f0e }--

